description: Defines investment domain data models including Deal, Evidence, Document, and Analysis entities with relationships and state transitions.
## Core Data Models
### Deal Entity (Importance: 95)
- Investment deal lifecycle tracking 
- Stage progression: intake -> under_review -> in_diligence -> ready_decision -> pitched
- Required confidence thresholds per stage
- Deal intelligence versioning through DIO objects
- Parent-child relationship tracking for deal evolution
### Evidence Entity (Importance: 90)
- Structured evidence collection for investment decisions
- Types: fact, metric, quote, document
- Classification: market, team, financial, risk, competition, product
- Confidence scoring system
- Source document linking and traceability
### Document Entity (Importance: 85)
- Investment document classification system
- Categories: pitch_deck, financials, product, legal, team, market
- Processing status tracking
- Document relationship mapping
- Version control and lineage tracking
### Analysis Entity (Importance: 90)
- Multi-cycle analysis framework
- Decision recommendations (GO/NO-GO/CONDITIONAL)  
- Confidence scoring per analysis dimension
- Evidence aggregation and validation
- Risk assessment tracking
### Report Entity (Importance: 80)
- Due diligence report generation
- Section organization and requirements
- Evidence coverage tracking
- Recommendation synthesis
- Multi-format export support
## Relationships
Deal <-> Evidence: Many-to-many tracking of supporting evidence
Deal <-> Document: Many-to-many document associations
Deal <-> Analysis: One-to-many analysis cycles
Analysis <-> Evidence: Many-to-many evidence validation
## State Transitions
1. Deal Stage Progression
- Intake: Initial document collection
- Under Review: Basic analysis complete
- In Diligence: Detailed analysis ongoing
- Ready Decision: Analysis complete, meets confidence threshold
- Pitched: Final decision made
2. Document Processing
- Uploaded -> Processing -> Analyzed -> Verified
- Failed states handled with error tracking
- Reprocessing triggers for quality issues
3. Analysis Cycles  
- Phase 1: Initial scoring
- Phase 2: Detailed analysis with evidence
- Phase 3: Final recommendation
- Each phase requires confidence threshold

